70
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,800
or when the goal is vague,

71
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,800
and keep fruitlessly trying to solve the wrong problem.

72
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,240
But the concept is really interesting, though.

73
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,720
Instead of just telling it to "fix this one bug," you can give Codex a goal.

74
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,610
You could give Codex a goal.

75
00:03:15,610 --> 00:03:18,530
For example, "Improve the test coverage for this authentication module."

76
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:20,890
Or, 'Keep working through this migration until the build passes.'

77
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,240
